<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42143" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saccārĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		saccus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to sacks</i>,
				<i>sack-</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: navis, perh. <i>laden with
				sacks</i>, Auct. ap. <i><span class="en">Quint. 8, 2,
			13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Substt.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sac-cārĭus</span></b> , ii,
			m., <i>one who carries sacks</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 18, 1, 40, § 3</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
			4176</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sac-cārĭa</span></b> ,
				ae,f., <i>the labor of a
				porter</i>, <i><span class="en">App. M. 1, p. 36 <i>fin.</i></span></i> (al. sagariam).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
